From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtual-media: fix inactivity timer, stats, and large ISO
 cdrom limit

Three fixes for virtual media on platforms without the AMI stats kernel
patch:

1) active_state.hpp: lastAccess is default-initialized to epoch (time
   zero).  The inactivity timer checks (now - lastAccess) >= 1800s on
   the very first 1-second tick.  Since now - epoch is always >>1800s,
   every mount is immediately unmounted.  Fix: initialize lastAccess
   to steady_clock::now() so the timer counts from mount time.

2) system.hpp getStats(): The kernel f_mass_storage function has no
   "stats" sysfs attribute (that is an AMI kernel addition).  getStats()
   returns empty and logs an error every second, spamming the journal.
   Fix: when the stats file doesn't exist, return a monotonic counter
   so the inactivity timer sees continuous "activity" and never fires
   due to missing stats.

3) system.hpp configure(): detectImageType() correctly identifies
   ISO9660 images via the "CD001" signature and sets cdrom=1.  However,
   the kernel mass storage cdrom mode caps images at 256*60*75 sectors
   (~562MB).  DVD/Blu-ray ISOs (>700MB) are silently truncated.  Fix:
   force cdrom=0 for images larger than 700MB.

Signed-off-by: local <local@local>
---
 src/state/active_state.hpp | 3 ++-
 src/system.hpp             | 13 ++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/state/active_state.hpp b/src/state/active_state.hpp
--- a/src/state/active_state.hpp
+++ b/src/state/active_state.hpp
@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@
     std::unique_ptr<resource::Process> process;
     std::unique_ptr<resource::Gadget> gadget;
     std::function<void(const boost::system::error_code&)> handler;
-    std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::steady_clock> lastAccess;
+    std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::steady_clock> lastAccess =
+        std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     std::string lastStats;
 };
diff --git a/src/system.hpp b/src/system.hpp
--- a/src/system.hpp
+++ b/src/system.hpp
@@ -1254,7 +1254,11 @@
                     return -1;
                 }

-                echoToFile(funcMassStorageDir / "lun.0/cdrom", (imgType == 1) ? "1" : "0");
+                // The kernel USB mass storage cdrom mode caps images at
+                // 256*60*75 sectors (~562MB).  Force cdrom=0 for images
+                // larger than 700MB so the full image is exposed.
+                bool useCdrom = (imgType == 1) && (imageSize <= 700ULL * 1024 * 1024);
+                echoToFile(funcMassStorageDir / "lun.0/cdrom", useCdrom ? "1" : "0");
                 echoToFile(funcMassStorageDir / "lun.0/file", path);
                 /*usbVmediaName visible in host is posted to inquiry_string*/
 		snprintf(usbVmediaName, USB_VMEDIA_NAME_SIZE, "Virtual USB %s", name.c_str());
@@ -1575,8 +1579,11 @@
         std::ifstream ifs(statsPath);
         if (!ifs.is_open())
         {
-            LogMsg(Logger::Error, name, "Failed to open ", statsPath);
-            return {};
+            // The kernel stats attribute is not available on all
+            // platforms.  Return a monotonic counter so the inactivity
+            // timer sees continuous "activity" and never fires.
+            static uint64_t fakeCounter = 0;
+            return std::to_string(fakeCounter++);
         }

         return std::string{std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(ifs),
--
2.25.1
